adjudication.rationale:
The diff adds a feature-flag guard around all removal-event cleanup in `AdminPermissions.registerListener`:
```java
if (Profile.isFeatureEnabled(Profile.Feature.ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ)) {
  if (event instanceof RoleRemovedEvent) { ... setPermissionsEnabled(role,false); }
  else if (event instanceof ClientRemovedEvent) { ... setPermissionsEnabled(client,false); }
  else if (event instanceof GroupRemovedEvent) { ... setPermissionsEnabled(group,false); }
}
```
Previously this cleanup ran unconditionally. With the feature disabled, removals will no longer trigger `setPermissionsEnabled(..., false)`, so any existing fine-grained permission artifacts created earlier will not be cleaned up on entity deletion, matching the finding’s “orphaned permission data” concern.
